# What EAS leaves OUT of the project archive it uploads to build.
#
# CAREFUL: when this file exists, EAS uses it INSTEAD OF .gitignore, not in
# addition to it. So it has to repeat everything .gitignore says — otherwise
# node_modules, the generated android/ folder and the downloaded signing
# credentials all get uploaded. Keep the two in step; the only intended
# difference is the `store/` block at the bottom.

# dependencies
node_modules/

# Expo
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts

# Native
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# Signing credentials pulled down with `eas credentials`. The .jks is covered
# above, but credentials.json holds the keystore + key PASSWORDS in plaintext.
# A cloud build must never receive these: EAS holds the keystore server-side
# and signs with it there.
credentials.json
credentials/

# Metro
.metro-health-check*

# debug
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.pem

# local env files
.env*.local

# Firebase credentials
# google-services.json is intentionally NOT ignored (the build requires it)
GoogleService-Info.plist

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# generated native folders. These matter more here than in git: shipping a
# populated android/ makes EAS treat the project as bare and skip prebuild, so
# it would build the locally-generated native project — including the local
# signing config, which references gradle properties that only exist on this
# machine.
/ios
/android
modules/*/android/build/
modules/*/android/.gradle/

# ── The only thing this file adds over .gitignore ──────────────────────────
# Store listing artwork, review stills and screenshot sources: tracked in git
# (they are real work), but no build reads them, and they are ~64 MB of the
# upload. Anything else non-runtime should go under store/ rather than earn a
# new rule here.
store/
